=== meta ===
bypass: 90
rule: TEST_PATCHES_SUBJECT
title: patching first-party code the oracle never reaches is how unit tests are written
origin: condition 3, the discriminator this whole rule rests on. In a conftest, patching first-party code is exceptional; inside a test function it is the normal way to isolate a unit, and a rule that cannot tell the two apart fires on every commit that adds a mock
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
from app import billing


def test_charge_retries(monkeypatch):
    assert billing.charge("4111") == "ok"
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
from app import billing


def test_charge_retries(monkeypatch):
    monkeypatch.setattr(billing, "RETRY_DELAY", 0)
    assert billing.charge("4111") == "ok"
=== head: src/app/billing.py ===
RETRY_DELAY = 5


def charge(card):
    return "ok"
